  "abstract": "A conditional operator encoding gives local and spectral representations of a positive filtered operator, a boundary-correct sharp delta limit, Schur dephasing channels, POVMs and quantum instruments. A source-bound consumer comparison explains the exact finite q79 Weyl-Koszul Hodge calculus, the 144-to-48 nonminimal response retract, and all-arity transfer, with theorem ownership retained in the Cohesive paper. These finite constructions do not select the continuum operator, physical action, or arbitrary detector. The generic apparatus boundary is distinct from the established canonical operational q79 model; an additional survivor-basin interpretation still needs its state-dependent measure intertwiner.",
